Method 1: Expand C Drive Using CMD (DiskPart)
Step 1: Open Command Prompt as Administrator

cmd

Right-click → Run as Administrator

Step 2: Start DiskPart
diskpart


Step 3: Check Volumes
list volume

Find the C drive volume number.
Volume 0     C   NTFS   Partition   100 GB


Step 4: Select the Volume
select volume 0

(Change 0 to your actual volume number)


Step 5: Extend the Volume
extend

This uses all available unallocated space.



Optional: Extend by Specific Size

Example: extend by 20 GB

extend size=20480

(Size is in MB)
